      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14194746/assets/5355859a0307e46ae84d12bc5e0b183d72458972c8a417fb6d9296b4769ea078.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=g(x)$ is shown above. \nApproximate $g'(x)$ at the point $x=4$ using a central difference approximation with step size $h=4.$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\ng'(x) \\approx \\dfrac{g(x+h) - g(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \n\nat the point $x=4$ with step size $h=4.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(4) & ≈\\frac{g(4+4)-g(4-4)}{2(4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(8)-g(0)}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4-(-10)}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{8} \\\\  & =0.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
